# Power: lower the per-codec clock requests during playback.
#
# Clock manager (mod00): modules request rows of the table at 0x03076324
# (36 rows x 0x1C: id, PLL, A core, A hclk, A pclk, B core, B bus; Hz) via
# FUN_0306aee4(id) / release FUN_0306af30(id). FUN_0306ad00 SUMS the rows of all
# active ids, raises each field to row 1 (96 MHz floor) and caps at row 35. The
# music service picks the codec row at mod33 0x03080c24 (by codec type 0x03039e94)
# on top of row 3 (48 MHz A fields) and row 4 (MusicInit, 48 MHz everywhere).
#
# Stock result: A core ~225-232 MHz, B (decode) core 348-450 MHz for every format,
# WAV included; pause keeps it. No voltage scaling exists, so this saves dynamic
# power only. New rows: A fields 0 (the A core gets the 96 MHz floor, same as the
# UI), PLL 0 (solver picks it), B core as below (+48 from row 4). EQ rows 23-25
# still add on top. APE / OGG high rates / DSD (rows 17, 18, 21, 22) unchanged.
#
#   format          B core stock -> new   (simulated solver output)
#   MP3/WMA/AAC/WAV 348-450      -> 144   PLL 288, A 96
#   OGG (rows 14-16) 448         -> 240   PLL 480, A 96
#   FLAC/ALAC        448-450     -> 288   PLL 288, A 96

